    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In order to test whether the observed data are consistent with a specified vector q of population frequencies, we need the value of the likelihood function under this constraint. Denoting the expected value for the number of individuals in category i by $ \\widehat{n}_{i} = q_{i}n $, we can write $ q_{i} = \\widehat{n}_{i}/n $. Substitution into Equation A4.10a gives the likelihood under q as",
